    {
      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To find the probability of choosing 2 girls when 2 members are chosen out of 10, we use the concept of combinations.\n\nThe total number of ways to choose 2 members out of 10 is: \n\\[ \\binom{10}{2} = \\frac{10!}{2!(10-2)!} = \\frac{10 \\times 9}{2 \\times 1} = 45 \\]\n\nThe number of ways to choose 2 girls out of 5 girls is:\n\\[ \\binom{5}{2} = \\frac{5!}{2!(5-2)!} = \\frac{5 \\times 4}{2 \\times 1} = 10 \\]\n\nThe probability is then the ratio of the number of ways to choose 2 girls to the total number of ways to choose 2 members:\n\\[ \\text{Probability} = \\frac{\\binom{5}{2}}{\\binom{10}{2}} = \\frac{10}{45} = \\frac{2}{9} \\]\n\nTherefore, the probability that the two chosen members are both girls is \\(\\boxed{\\frac{2}{9}}\\).",
